@meta
id: 19-15
title: Errors into the list
chapter: 19
type: lesson
skills: make-errorformat
par: 77
minutes: 7
vscode: the Problems panel
vimrc: set errorformat=%f(%l\\,%c):\ %m hidden
open: tsc-output.txt

@brief
The quickfix list was built for compiler errors; search results came
later. In front of you is `tsc-output.txt`, the saved output of a `tsc`
run: three errors, one per line, each in the form
`file(line,col): message`. `:cfile tsc-output.txt` reads it into the
quickfix list and jumps to the first error with the cursor on the exact
column. `:cn` walks the rest. It is the Problems panel, except the
cursor is put where the problem is.

Vim has to be told the shape of a line to read a file, line and column
out of it. That is `errorformat`, a small pattern language: `%f` file,
`%l` line, `%c` column, `%m` message, and literal characters for the
rest. For tsc it is `%f(%l,%c): %m`, and it is set for this lesson. The
default `errorformat` knows gcc and a few others; it does not know
tsc, and without the option every line would load as a message with
no file behind it and `:cn` would have nowhere to go.

Fix all three. Each is a short edit at the cursor, and the message
tells you what it should be. The output file itself must not change.

@keys
| `:cfile file` | load errors from a file, jump to the first |
| `:cgetfile file` | load without jumping |
| `errorformat` | how to read `file`, `line`, `col` and `message` out of each line |
| `%f %l %c %m` | file, line, column, message |

@hints
`:cfile tsc-output.txt`. The first error says `sendRefund` does not
exist and suggests `issueRefund`; the cursor is on the word.
--
`ciw` and the suggested name, `:w`, `:cn`. Error two is `args.orderId`
where the type only has `id`. Error three compares a number to a
string: `'200'` should be `200`.
--
For the third the cursor lands at the start of the comparison. `f'`
finds the opening quote, `x` removes it, `f'` `x` again for the other.
`:wq`.

@solution
    :cfile tsc-output.txt<Enter>
    ciw issueRefund <Esc> :w<Enter> :cn<Enter>
    ciw id <Esc> :w<Enter> :cn<Enter>
    f' x f' x :wq<Enter>

`errorformat` is a scanf for compiler output. `%f(%l,%c): %m` says:
some file, a paren, a line number, a comma, a column, a paren, a colon,
a space, and the rest is the message. Writing it down takes two
layers of escaping. Inside the option a bare comma separates
alternative formats, so a literal comma is `\,`; and `:set` itself
strips one backslash and stops at an unescaped space, so the line in a
vimrc reads `set errorformat=%f(%l\\,%c):\ %m`. That is the one to put
in `after/ftplugin/typescript.vim` if you want it permanently, or use
`:compiler tsc`, which ships with vim and sets it for you.

`:cfile` jumps to the first error. `:cgetfile` loads the same list
without moving, for when you want `:copen` and a read before touching
anything. Both take any file in the right format, which is what makes
a saved build log or a CI artefact just as usable as a live run.

The next lesson runs the build from inside vim instead of reading a
file.

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.sendRefund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.issueRefund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@start src/domain/order/order.resolver.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';

@injectable()
export class OrderResolver {
  constructor(@inject(OrderProvider) protected orderProvider: OrderProvider) {}

  public async order(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.findOne(args.orderId);
  }

  public async cancelOrder(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.cancel(args.id);
  }
}

@expected src/domain/order/order.resolver.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';

@injectable()
export class OrderResolver {
  constructor(@inject(OrderProvider) protected orderProvider: OrderProvider) {}

  public async order(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.findOne(args.id);
  }

  public async cancelOrder(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.cancel(args.id);
  }
}

@start src/domain/payment/payment.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { PaymentRepository } from './payment.repository';
import { PaymentProducer } from './payment.producer';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class PaymentProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(PaymentRepository) protected paymentRepository: PaymentRepository,
    @inject(PaymentProducer) protected paymentProducer: PaymentProducer,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async reverse(id: string) {
    const payment = await this.paymentRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!payment) {
      throw exception('PAYMENT_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    const receipt = await this.paymentService.issueRefund(payment.orderId);

    await this.paymentProducer.refundIssued({ paymentId: id, receipt });

    return receipt;
  }
}

@start src/infrastructure/services/payment.service.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { HttpClient } from '../http/http.client';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  constructor(@inject(HttpClient) protected http: HttpClient) {}

  public async issueRefund(orderId: string) {
    const response = await this.http.post('/issueRefund', { orderId });

    if (response.status !== '200') {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}

@expected src/infrastructure/services/payment.service.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { HttpClient } from '../http/http.client';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  constructor(@inject(HttpClient) protected http: HttpClient) {}

  public async issueRefund(orderId: string) {
    const response = await this.http.post('/issueRefund', { orderId });

    if (response.status !== 200) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}

